# Design without guessing

**[Read the published handbook](https://maxiplux.github.io/maxiplux-skills/)** · **[Open the offline HTML](./guide-lines.html)** — three connected parts, with enlarged image viewing, diagrams, comparison tables, copyable prompts and offline reading.

| Part | Your main question | Editable source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **01 · UI / UX & Design** | Can a person understand and complete the task? | [UI / UX & Design](./ui-ux-design.md) |
| **02 · AI Agents** | What should the model decide, and what must code control? | [AI Agents](./ai-agents.md) |
| **03 · Software Architecture** | Who owns behavior, data and failure paths? | [Software Architecture](./software-architecture.md) |

Follow the same invoice example through all three: paste text, extract an editable draft, correct it, and explicitly create an invoice. A skill guides the coding agent; it does not install a running model or replace the application's contracts.

The UI part covers Taste, Impeccable, getdesign.md and Web Design Guidelines. The AI part separates coding agents from runtime agents and explains Spring AI, tools, context, evaluation and limits. The architecture part covers Spring VSA, Angular boundaries, transactions, errors, installation and the complete delivery workflow.

